==Linguistics==
{{Main|Qymishization}}

In linguistics, the term [[qymishization]] was coined to refer to the adoption or borrowing of words from the [[Qymish language]] by other linguistic groups. In languages with non-Sukatic alphabets, these borrowed words can be written in the [[Sukatic script]] anyway, resulting in a text made up of a mixture of scripts; other times they are transliterated. 

It may also refer to the replacement of borrowed foreign words in the [[Qymish language]] by Qymish constructions, in which case names of objects or people can be qymishified. 

